#!/bin/bash
set -e
perl -0pi -e 's/An artifact is indexed exactly while it is complete, the completeness the\nper-source counters use: its entry exists and neither the entry nor its manifest\nretirement state is marked evicted\./An artifact is indexed exactly while the store holds all of its bytes: its entry\nexists, the entry is not marked evicted, and its manifest retirement state has\nneither evicted it nor retired any chunk. This is stricter than the per-source\ncounters\x27 completeness, which looks only at the evicted flags: expiry retires an\nartifact\x27s chunks at its deadline and keeps the entry a day longer, and the index\nalready does not list it in that window./' interfaces.md
perl -0pi -e 's/- expiry deletes an artifact entry \(an artifact with records, in the batch that\n  deletes its first due record; a recordless artifact, with its time-index key\);\n- pressure eviction marks an artifact evicted through its manifest retirement\n  state, or deletes a recordless artifact entry;/- expiry retires an artifact\x27s chunks at its deadline (the manifest retirement\n  state records the retired chunks), and the key goes in that batch; the entry is\n  deleted a day later, or with its time-index key for a recordless artifact;\n- pressure eviction marks an artifact evicted or retires its chunks through its\n  manifest retirement state, or deletes a recordless artifact entry;/' interfaces.md
perl -0pi -e 's/artifact entry is never created, retired \(evicted through its\nmanifest retirement state\) or deleted/artifact entry is never created, retired (its bytes released through its\nmanifest retirement state, at expiry or eviction) or deleted/' architecture.md
